# Node version pinning — mechanical enforcement of the 22.x-only policy.
#
# `engines` in package.json is only ADVISORY by default (npm prints an
# EBADENGINE warning and installs anyway). engine-strict turns that warning
# into a hard install failure, so a wrong Node version cannot silently
# produce a build. Every environment must be on Node 22.x:
#   .nvmrc, all .github/workflows/* (node-version: '22'), Dockerfile
#   (node:22-alpine), and the engines block in every workspace package.json.
#
# The TYPES must match the runtime too: `@types/node` is pinned to ^22.20.1 in
# BOTH the root and apps/host package.json. They are deliberately the SAME
# string so npm hoists exactly one copy — when they diverged (root ^26,
# apps/host ^25) npm nested a second copy under apps/host/node_modules and
# tsc happily accepted Node 25/26 APIs that do not exist on the pinned 22.x
# runtime. Keep both specs identical.
#
# IMPORTANT — this flag applies to the WHOLE dependency tree, not just our
# own packages. npm refuses to install if ANY transitive dependency declares
# an incompatible engines range. The current tree's tightest constraint is:
#
#   posthog-node@5.33.4  ->  "node": "^20.20.0 || >=22.22.0"
#
# so the effective floor is Node >= 22.22.0 (latest 22.x is 22.23.2).
# Node 22.0-22.21 will FAIL `npm ci` here. If a CI runner, Docker base image,
# or the Vercel build image ever resolves "22.x" to a minor below 22.22.0,
# installs break — re-check this floor when bumping posthog-node.
#
# Two mitigations keep every environment ABOVE that floor:
#   1. `.nvmrc` pins the EXACT version (22.23.2), not the bare major, so
#      `nvm use` locally cannot land on a 22.0-22.21 that is already
#      installed on the machine.
#   2. Every actions/setup-node step sets `check-latest: true`. Without it
#      setup-node prefers the runner image's TOOL CACHE, so a runner that
#      ever caches a 22.x below 22.22.0 would hard-fail `npm ci` in all 13
#      workflows at once with no prior warning. check-latest makes setup-node
#      consult the Node dist manifest and fetch the newest 22.x instead.
# Both are re-derived, not restated: REG-378 recomputes this floor from
# package-lock.json and fails if the number above goes stale.
#
# To temporarily unblock an install, set engine-strict=false (do not delete
# this file silently — the pin is the point).
engine-strict=true
